PUBLIC RESPONSE: There is no verifiable year because there is no credible primary evidence that Goodluck Ebele Jonathan ever publicly self-identified as “Goodluck Ebele Azikiwe Jonathan”.

His legal/official name across the authoritative record is consistently Goodluck Ebele Jonathan:
* INEC Form CF001 and nomination papers;
* affidavits of age / passport particulars;
* sworn oaths of office as Vice President 29 May 2007-2010 and as President 17 May 2010 and 29 May 2011-2015;
* official Gazette notices and state records.

“Azikiwe” does not appear in any of those primary sources, in a verified speech transcript, official press release or gazette notice in which Jonathan states his own name as including Azikiwe. The “Goodluck Ebele Azikiwe Jonathan” form is an internet/partisan embellishment that circulates as a mark of respect to Nnamdi Azikiwe.

The only dated story repeatedly cited is the March 2011 Enugu campaign stop in the run-up to the 2011 presidential election, where it is second-hand reported that Jonathan introduced himself to an Igbo audience with an expanded form of his name for local goodwill. That anecdote has never been substantiated with contemporaneous audio/video, a verbatim transcript or a reliable news report quoting a self-introduction as “Goodluck Ebele Azikiwe Jonathan”, and it was never followed by any formal name change, INEC affidavit, passport amendment or other official documentation. Jonathan’s official records remained Goodluck Ebele Jonathan before and after 2011.

The 2007 anchor linked to selection as Yar’Adua’s running mate / vice-presidential swearing-in is also unsupported by primary sources; contemporary 2007 oaths, INEC filings and Gazette notices list Goodluck Ebele Jonathan only.

In factual terms the premise is false: no documented public self-identification as Azikiwe exists on record, and therefore no year can be assigned.

